<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Using Power Properties for Exponents</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01242</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Using Power Properties for Exponents</md:title>
    <md:uuid>36692d0b-e17f-4240-b529-ccdbd4dc1bc9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Work with a partner to complete the activity. Discuss any differences in
        the simplified results you find. Make sure you both understand each step you take to
        simplify.</para>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Quotient to a Negative Power Property</title>
  
  <para id="para-00003">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are real numbers, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is an integer, then</para>
  <para id="para-00004"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para></note>

      <para id="para-00005">Complete problems 1 - 3 using the product property for exponents. Double
        click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00006" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">1. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">


          <para id="para-00007"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>807</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>243</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00008" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">2. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">


          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00010"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00011" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">3. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">


          <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00013"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <note id="note-00002">
        <title>Power Property for Exponents</title>
  
  <para id="para-00015">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a real number and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are integers, then</para>
  <para id="para-00016"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para></note>

      <para id="para-00017">Complete problems 4 - 6 using the power property for exponents. Double
        click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00018" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">4. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">


          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00020"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>048</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>576</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00021" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">5. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">


          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00023"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>21</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00024" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">6. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">


          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00026"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>64</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <note id="note-00003">
        <title>Product to a Power Property for Exponents</title>
  
  <para id="para-00028"> If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are real numbers and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a whole number, then</para>
  <para id="para-00029"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para></note>

      <para id="para-00030">Complete problems 7 - 9 using the product to a power property for
        exponents.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00031" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">7. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">


          <para id="para-00032">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00033"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>128</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>v</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00034" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">8. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">


          <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00036"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>024</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00037" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">9. </span><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">


          <para id="para-00038">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00039"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <para id="para-00040">Choose one example above and explain each step to your partner. Listen
        as your partner does the same for you.</para>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00004">
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00041"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_5_1_4_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>

      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title> Quotient to a Negative Power Property</title>
        <para id="para-00043">Suppose now we have a fraction raised to a negative exponent. Let’s
          use our definition of negative exponents to lead us to a new property.</para>
        <para id="para-00044"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00045"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Use the definition of a negative
          exponent, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          .</para>
        <para id="para-00002">
          <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00046"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Simplify the denominator.</para>
        <para id="para-00042"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00047"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify the complex fraction.</para>
        <para id="para-00110"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00111">But we know that <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00048"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - This tells us that</para>
        <para id="para-00112"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00049">To get from the original fraction raised to a negative exponent to the
          final result, we took the reciprocal of the base—the fraction—and changed the sign of the
          exponent.</para>
        <para id="para-00050">This leads us to the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">Quotient
          to a Negative Power Property</term>.</para>
        <note id="note-00005">
          <title>Quotient to a Negative Power Property</title>
      
      <para id="para-00052">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are real numbers, <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is an integer, then</para>
      <para id="para-00053"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para></note>
        <para id="para-00054">Now that we have negative exponents, we can use the Product Property
          we learned in Activity 5.1.2 with expressions that have negative exponents, too.</para>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Power Property for Exponents</title>
        <para id="para-00055">Now let’s look at an exponential expression that contains a power
          raised to a power. See if you can discover a general property.</para>
        <para id="para-00056">

          <media alt="A chart explains that the value of (x squared) raised to the power of 3 means multiplying x squared three times, resulting in a total of 6 x factors; equals x to the power of 6¶.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_03_11_01.jpg" width="550"/>
          </media>

        </para>
        <para id="para-00057">Notice the 6 is the <emphasis effect="italics">product</emphasis> of
          the exponents, 2 and 3. We see that <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          or <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00058">We multiplied the exponents. This leads to the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">Power Property for Exponents</term>.</para>
        <note id="note-00006">
          <title>Power Property for Exponents</title>
      
      <para id="para-00060">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is a real number and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are integers, then</para>
      <para id="para-00061"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para><para id="para-00062">To raise a power to a power, multiply the exponents.</para>
        </note>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00005">
        <title> Product to a Power Property for Exponents</title>
        <para id="para-00063">We will now look at an expression containing a product that is raised
          to a power. Can you find this pattern?</para>
        <para id="para-00064"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00065"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - What does this mean?</para>
        <para id="para-00113"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00066"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - We group the like factors together.</para>
        <para id="para-00114"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00067"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - How many factors of 2 and of<m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>?</para>
        <para id="para-00115"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00068">Notice that each factor was raised to the power and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00069">The exponent applies to each of the factors. This leads to the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00003">Product to a Power Property for Exponents</term>
          .</para>
        <note id="note-00007">
          <title>Product to a Power Property for Exponents</title>
      
      <para id="para-00071">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are real numbers and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is a whole number, then</para>
      <para id="para-00072"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para><para id="para-00073">To raise a product to a power, raise each factor to that power.</para>
        </note>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00006">
        <title> Quotient to a Power Property for Exponents</title>
        <para id="para-00074">Now we will look at an example that will lead us to the Quotient to a
          Power Property.</para>
        <para id="para-00075"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00076"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - This means</para>
        <para id="para-00116"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00077"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Multiply the fractions.</para>
        <para id="para-00117"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00078"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Write with exponents.</para>
        <para id="para-00118"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00079">Notice that the exponent applies to both the numerator and the
          denominator.</para>
        <para id="para-00080">We see that <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
          .</para>
        <para id="para-00081">This leads to the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00004">Quotient
          to a Power Property for Exponents</term>.</para>
        <note id="note-00008">
          <title>Quotient to a Power Property for Exponents</title>
      
      <para id="para-00083">If <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are real numbers, <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is an integer, then</para>
      <para id="para-00084"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para><para id="para-00085">To raise a fraction to a power, raise the numerator and denominator to
          that power.</para>
        </note>
        <note class="try" id="note-00009">
          <title>Using Power Properties for Exponents</title>
    <para id="para-00086">Simplify
          each expression using the property identified.</para>
    
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
            <problem id="prob-00010">
              <para id="para-00087">Use the Quotient to a Negative Power Property for Exponents.</para>
              <para id="para-00088">1. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00089">2. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00090">Use the Power Property for Exponents.</para>
              <para id="para-00091">3. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00092">4. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00093">5. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00094">Use the Product to a Power Property for Exponents.</para>
              <para id="para-00095">6. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00096">7. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00097">Use the Quotient to a Power Property for Exponents.</para>
              <para id="para-00098">8. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00099">9. <m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mrow>
                            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:mrow>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00100"/>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00010">
              <para id="para-00101">Compare your answers:</para>
              <para id="para-00102">Here is how to simplify the expressions:</para>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                          <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>807</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>243</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>s</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>15</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>64</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>h</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>24</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>64</m:mn>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                          <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>64</m:mn>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>

                <item><m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></item>
              </list>
              <para id="para-00103"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Use Quotient to a Power Property, <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                          <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                          <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para><para id="para-00014"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00104"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Use the Product to a Power
          Property, <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para><para id="para-00027"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00051">9. <m:math>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                      <m:mfrac>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                            <m:mrow>
                              <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                            </m:mrow>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:msup>
                            <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          </m:msup>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:mfrac>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00105"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Use Quotient to a Power Property, <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                          <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                          <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para><para id="para-00059"> <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mrow>
                            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:mrow>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00106"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Use the Product to a Power
          Property,<m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para><para id="para-00070"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mrow>
                            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                          </m:mrow>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00107"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify using the Power Property,<m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para><para id="para-00082"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mrow>
                            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                            <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                          </m:mrow>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00108"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Use the definition of negative
          exponent.</para><para id="para-00119"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00109"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Simplify.</para><para id="para-00120"><m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>

  </content>
